WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.835
-My guest tonight is the mayor
of the great city of Atlanta

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:05.071
Please welcome to the show
Mayor Keisha Lance Bottoms

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mayor, thank you so much
for making time for us today

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to start by a speec
you gave last week.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:15.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
You spoke both as a mayor
and as a mother.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was passionate.
It felt very honest.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:22.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
How hard has it been for you
to address your city

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.791 line:92%
in this really trying time

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, what you got from
me on Friday, Seth,

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
was every emotion
that I've been feeling

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.766 line:92%
over the past week or so.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you got it unfiltered
on Friday.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.104 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And like so many people,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
we all have so many emotions
about this.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:44.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
And whether it's watching it
feeling it in ourselves,

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.678 line:92%
or watching it with our kids

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
or our communities,
I had a platform Friday

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:52.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
just to express what I fel
and that frustration.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:57.624
And I can tell you, I didn't
plan on saying any of that

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.894
I didn't know what I was going
to say when I said it on Friday.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.595 line:92%
And in fact, after I was done,

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
I couldn't remember
what I had said.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think, you know,
it really speaks to

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:14.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
how built up and just
how full I felt on Friday.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:20.780
But I'm just grateful that i
resonated with so many people.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.348 line:92%
-You have made the point,

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I think a lot
of people would share,

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the president
should stop talking.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.021 size:84% position:42%
When he talks, it's not
particularly helpful.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
He obviously spoke last nigh
about the need

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:33.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
for law enforcement to dominat
the people in the streets.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you both
protect your city

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:39.666
and communicate with your
law enforcement officers

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:44.337
as to how to move forward with
what's happening in your city?

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a really
delicate balance,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:51.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
and ironically,
just as I was walking in her

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
to record with you,
I was speaking with

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:57.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
my 18-year-old son,
and he was telling me --

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:01.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
showing me another video,
and his frustration.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:04.791 size:88% position:44%
And what I was trying to
articulate to him was,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:09.395 size:81% position:41%
when I said on Friday,
"I can't protect you,"

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.997 line:92%
what I was expressing was that

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:14.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
our law enforcement
officers are tired.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
They are beyond exhausted
at this point.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.405 line:92%
They're working 18-hour shifts

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
to try and maintain some commo
stability in our cities.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:27.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we understand the
frustration and the anger,

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:31.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all of these emotions
that people are experiencing

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.318 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
right now.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.453 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It's understandable.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
But on the other side of this,
you also have

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.225 size:81% position:41%
many of our officers,
especially in Atlanta,

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.793 line:92%
who are African-American men

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.396 size:75% position:38%
who are experiencing
these same emotions.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:47.267
They're experiencing it becaus
of who they are and the children

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they also are raising
in this country.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:55.842 line:92%
And...it's a difficult balance

00:02:55.842 --> 00:03:00.947
Showing that support, asking
our officers to show restraint

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:05.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
and compassion, while also
trying to maintain

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
some type of order
in our streets

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.355 size:75% position:38%
when we have so many
peaceful protesters.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.926
But we have so many other people
who are just attempting

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:16.529 line:92%
to be disrupters right now

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:20.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You and the chief of police
made the decision

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
to fire two police officer
after watching video

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of their behavior.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:30.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you balance both
supporting police officers

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:34.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
and making sure you remove
the bad actors

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.014 size:88% position:44% line:92%
within the police force?

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:39.018
Because it does strike me that
what everybody wants to believe,

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
what all citizens
want to believe,

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
that if there are bad
police officers,

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'll be removed
from the force.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that hopefully the messag
that comes across

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you make
a decision like that?

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:50.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It certainly is.
And the reality is that,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:53.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
had this incident happened
last week,

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:56.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
we probably would have taken
a little more time

00:03:56.603 --> 00:04:00.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
to look at what happened
with this incident

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.908 line:92%
and with these officers and --

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
but what we've seen over
the past week is,

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
we don't have the luxury
of time anymore.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.082 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We have to act swiftly,

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:12.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially when it's very clea
that our officers

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:14.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
are not behaving
appropriately.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:18.524
And I think that is what's to be
expected or should be expected

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
from so many of us
across the country now.

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:26.633
And it's also a culture shif
for many of our police officers,

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:31.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they have to understand
that they won't always

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:35.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
have another chance
to get it right.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:38.011 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And again, it's a shift

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:41.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we saw the Obama/Bide
administration making

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:45.985
when they left the handboo
on 21st Century Policing.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the same handbook --
it's a handbook

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:52.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they probably left
alongside the pandemic handboo

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:55.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Trump administratio
never picked up.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:58.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
But one of the major pillars
of 21st Century Policing

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:04.804
is that you create trustworthy
relationships with communities

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on the front end.

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, you do things like
we're doing in Atlanta,

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:12.211
where you have a center of hop
where our police recruits go

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
and volunteer and spend time
with the kids

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
so their first interaction
with them

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.252 line:92%
is not a negative interaction.

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:23.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where you have
implicit bias training.

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:25.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there were several pillars
to this program.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:30.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we've done a very good job
in Atlanta, by and large,

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:32.131 line:92%
in following those pillars

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's got to happen
across the country.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's got to come from
a national level

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.639 line:92%
in terms of expectations.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:42.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Someone else who spoke
passionately on stage with you

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
last Friday was the rapper
Killer Mike.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:48.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had incredibly
inspiring words.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
How does it come to pass
that you end up with a rappe

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.454 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on stage with you?

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:57.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, again,
these relationships

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.524 line:92%
are existing relationships

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:02.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
The irony, Killer Mike, T.I.
and I all went

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:03.529 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to the same high school.

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:06.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was a little ahead
of both of them,

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I'm a little
older than them.

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:11.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we bleed Atlanta.
We love Atlanta.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:15.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, Killer Mike and T.I.
worked on my transition

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:17.377 size:88% position:44% line:92%
when I went into office.

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:21.447
But -- and I could probably name
ten other celebrities

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Atlanta who've reached ou
and said,

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What is it that I could d
to help?"

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, this is not the first time
that Killer Mike

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:31.824
has been at the table with u
setting policy for our city,

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:34.594 size:78% position:39%
and having these real
conversations about

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:37.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we need to go
and how we need to approach it

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:40.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because again,
I look at everything

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.834 size:88% position:44% line:92%
as the lens of a mother.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:45.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I know I can say something
ten different ways

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:49.108 size:81% position:41%
and all my kids hear,
"Whomp, whomp, whomp."

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:53.045 size:84% position:42%
But if T.I. says it,
if Killer Mike says it,

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.515
it's going to translate,
and it's going to be heard

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's going to be felt
differently.

00:06:56.983 --> 00:07:01.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so on Friday, when
everything started to unrave

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:07.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Atlanta, I didn't have
a very clear picture

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:09.595 size:88% position:44% line:92%
of what we needed to do.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:12.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I knew the voices that
needed to be heard.

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:15.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's why you saw
Killer Mike, and Bernice King,

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:18.504 line:92%
and T.I., and Joe Beasley

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:22.708
and some other community leaders
standing with me.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:24.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I should make it clea
that while he's

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:28.548
one of my favorite rappers, he's
also an incredible activist.

00:07:28.548 --> 00:07:31.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that
really came through

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.985 line:92%
when he was on stage with you.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:36.289
You mentioned your older son
who just graduated high school

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:37.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
in quarantine,
is that correct?

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-You also --

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of your younger sons is,
I believe

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:43.996 size:78% position:39%
you've referred to it
as "Club Quarantine."

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:47.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's learning how to deeja
through this time?

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:49.569 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-He is and he loves it.

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:53.906 size:81% position:41%
He has a little corner
set up in my office.

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:57.376 size:88% position:44%
And now he even stays up
all night like a deejay.

00:07:57.376 --> 00:08:00.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I get up at 6:00 in
the morning to take a shower

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's taking a shower
to go to bed.

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:05.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we're going to have to und
some quarantine behaviors.

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:09.489
But yeah, it -- that's -- that's
been the upside of this.

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:11.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
Give all your kids our best.

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:14.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
And give our best
to the city of Atlanta.

00:08:14.627 --> 00:08:16.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
And best of luck
with everything.

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.097 size:81% position:41%
We really appreciate
the work you're doing.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And thank you so much for jus
giving me a platform

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:22.702 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to talk about this.

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:25.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I appreciate
your dedicating time

00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:27.840 line:92%
to these very real discussions

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
about where we are
in this country.

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:30.843 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I appreciate you.

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:32.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
Thank you, Mayor.

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:34.180 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

